    "md5": "871db139907790e56ff681f563c0b4c5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1875,
    "chunk_text": "HNB-Nucleus Software celebrate 5 years of partnership\n\nFrom left: Nucleus Software COO and Country Head Singapore Anurag Mantri, HNB EVP and Head of SME and Micro Finance Rajive Dissanayake, Nucleus Software co-founder and Managing Director Vishnu R. Dusad, HNB MD and CEO Damith Pallewatte, HNB COO Sanjay Wijemanne, Nucleus Software CBO Dr. Apurva Chamaria and HNB Chief Innovation Officer Chandima Cooray\n\nHatton National Bank PLC (HNB) and Nucleus Software, a global provider of lending and transaction banking solutions, celebrated five years of partnership at a gala evening held at ITC Ratnadipa, Colombo.\n\nThe milestone marks five years since HNB selected FinnAxia, Nucleus Software\u2019s flagship transaction banking platform, to modernise its corporate banking ecosystem and support the bank\u2019s long-term digital transformation vision.\n\nSince the partnership commenced in 2021, FinnAxia has played a pivotal role in strengthening HNB\u2019s transaction banking capabilities, enabling a seamless digital experience across vendor payments, payroll processing, bill payments, receivables, API banking, host-to-host connectivity and cross-border transactions.\n\nAll backed by strong MIS and customer relationship view on various fronts including CASA statements, loan details, term deposits to name a few. More importantly, it has helped HNB build the agility required to respond to the evolving customer expectations, accelerate service delivery and scale its transaction banking business in an increasingly digital-first environment.\n\nEvery single day, an average of over 3000 users leave their digital footprint on FinnAxia, a powerful testament to its adoption, reliability and value.\n\nThe platform enables straight-through processing across LankaPay payment rails, including CEFT, SLIPS and RTGS and facilitates LPOPP electronic bill payments for ASYCUDA, EPF and SLPA."
  },
